      "trigger": "depositFeeBps > 0 and feeRecipient != zero at the pinned identity source, with an otherwise valid positive deposit",
      "evidence": [
        "The verified StakedUSDat _deposit transfers ceil(assets*depositFeeBps/10000) separately to feeRecipient, then invokes super._deposit(caller,receiver,netAssets,shares).",
        "The superclass Deposit event records netAssets, while the admitted call input and total caller debit remain assets.",
        "The new Family reuses the standard verifiedDeposit predicate, whose lifecycleEventMatches call requires Deposit.assets == base.sampleAssets (the total call input).",
        "Therefore depositVerified is false whenever a positive fee is charged. Standard redeem is always reverted by this implementation, so standard.decide emits chain-proven-rejected / erc4626_execution_surfaces_failed."
      ],
      "required_fix": "Add Staked-owned fee-aware event proof at the same source, preserving full total-input debit, share receipt and supply-delta checks; keep the ordinary ERC4626 event equality strict. Verify nonzero-fee and zero-fee cases through the production identity lifecycle.",
      "validation_needed": [
        "Positive nonzero-fee deposit must admit exactly the deposit direction.",
        "Incorrect event net assets, missing fee/input debit, false shares and mixed-source fee evidence must fail.",
        "Existing ordinary, Custodian and InfiniFi identity/refresh contracts must retain their semantics."
      ],
      "actual_source_location": {
